From dfc13cc6be6563cc399d306887c2d8df294e001c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kiran Gopinathan <kiran@basis.ai>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 01:00:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] feat: Paralean hook 5, canonical instance names
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

With `canonicalInstNames`, instances the elaborator names are named
`<stock base without project suffix>_<first 8 hex of H("v0/insttype", text(τ))>`
for their final type τ, where H is Paralean's domain-separated hash
(SHA-256 of "paralean" NUL "v0/insttype" NUL ‖ uvarint length ‖ UTF-8 text),
never deduplicated with `_n` (a clash is an error):

* `instance` without a name (`elabDeclaration`): the name predicted from the
  header is used, checked against the final type, and the command is elaborated
  again only if they differ;
* deriving handlers (`mkInstName`, `applyDerivingHandlers`): the handler runs
  again under the canonical names if its instances' final types require it;
* delta deriving (`processDefDeriving`).

Every choice is logged with the stock name (`Lean.Paralean.takeInstNameLog`).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
